# The driver the phone's services are reached through. A system's own init
# mounts the filesystem that makes its nodes; a recovery's mounts none of
# it, and Skyward asks the services for the keys, the screen lock and the
# boot control through them. The nodes are given the modes ueventd's own
# table gives them, before anything that opens them starts.
on early-init
    mkdir /dev/binderfs 0755 root root
    mount binder binder /dev/binderfs
    chmod 0666 /dev/binderfs/binder
    chmod 0666 /dev/binderfs/hwbinder
    chmod 0666 /dev/binderfs/vndbinder
    symlink /dev/binderfs/binder /dev/binder
    symlink /dev/binderfs/hwbinder /dev/hwbinder
    symlink /dev/binderfs/vndbinder /dev/vndbinder
